five-headed dragon monster.

236
00:13:25,140 --> 00:13:26,160
Poor kid.

237
00:13:26,480 --> 00:13:29,297
There's no way he'll beat
that digital duelist now.

238
00:13:29,380 --> 00:13:30,210
Nope.

239
00:13:30,293 --> 00:13:31,175
There's not a chance.

240
00:13:31,440 --> 00:13:36,320
Our computer was programmed to mimic the
strategies of the world's best duelists.

241
00:13:37,160 --> 00:13:40,740
We've imported Seto's
deck and Yugi's, too.

242
00:13:41,400 --> 00:13:43,020
And it's got mine, right?

243
00:13:43,220 --> 00:13:45,860
Yeah, so it can lose,
too, just to be fair.

244
00:13:48,240 --> 00:13:52,000
But what fun is it to duel against
a computer that always wins?

245
00:13:52,360 --> 00:13:53,820
We thought about that.

246
00:13:54,120 --> 00:13:58,940
So we let players choose one of five
levels, from beginner all the way to expert.

247
00:13:59,420 --> 00:14:03,773
What an awesome way for kids to practice
dueling and improve their skills.

248
00:14:03,940 --> 00:14:08,587
Yes, a few more duels like this, and I
think Luke there could be a world champ.

249
00:14:10,020 --> 00:14:11,079
Commencing attack.

250
00:14:16,220 --> 00:14:17,180
Game over.

251
00:14:18,320 --> 00:14:19,560
Nice try, Luke.

252
00:14:19,740 --> 00:14:22,152
Looks like you owe me a blue-eyes burger.

253
00:14:22,240 --> 00:14:24,060
You put up a good fight, Luke.

254
00:14:24,280 --> 00:14:26,751
You just set your level a little too high.

255
00:14:26,840 --> 00:14:29,016
Hey, isn't that Yugi Moto over there?

256
