those theme park look-alikes.

257
00:14:31,960 --> 00:14:33,019
It's gotta be him!

258
00:14:33,300 --> 00:14:34,780
I'M GETTING AN AUTOGRAPH!

259
00:14:38,180 --> 00:14:40,600
It looks like someone's a celebrity.

260
00:14:40,940 --> 00:14:42,900
Well, I wouldn't go that far.

261
00:14:43,020 --> 00:14:45,400
I can't believe it's you!

262
00:14:45,600 --> 00:14:48,365
I've been a fan of yours
since Duelist Kingdom.

263
00:14:48,560 --> 00:14:50,180
By the way, I'm Leon.

264
00:14:52,300 --> 00:14:53,130
Hi, Leon!

265
00:14:53,220 --> 00:14:55,140
Hey, anyone want my autograph?

266
00:14:55,560 --> 00:14:57,897
Are we supposed to know you or something?

267
00:14:57,980 --> 00:14:59,200
Come on, kid!

268
00:14:59,400 --> 00:15:00,477
Jumpin' Joey Wheel!

269
00:15:00,560 --> 00:15:01,795
Battle City finalist?

270
00:15:02,520 --> 00:15:03,500
Joe, who?

271
00:15:04,120 --> 00:15:06,000
I'm sorry, but do I know you?

272
00:15:06,160 --> 00:15:07,880
I tell you, I get no respect.

273
00:15:08,480 --> 00:15:10,360
Excuse me, Mr. King of Games?

274
00:15:10,820 --> 00:15:12,600
Over here, sir. Uh, yeah?

275
00:15:13,060 --> 00:15:15,237
Can you take a look at my deck, please?

276
00:15:15,320 --> 00:15:18,144
No matter what I do, I
can't seem to win a duel.

277
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:20,900
Hmm, I see the problem.

278
00:15:21,200 --> 00:15:23,120
All you got are dragon cards.

279
00:15:23,400 --> 00:15:25,165
Yeah, dragons are my favorite.

280
00:15:25,320 --> 00:15:28,202
I traded all my magic and
trap cards to get them.

281
00:15:30,120 --> 00:15:36,180
Sure dragons are powerful, but you'll
never win with this deck Huh? Why not? Uh,

282
00:15:36,600 --> 00:15:41,160
that came out wrong Here's the deal
It's obvious that you value your cards,

283
00:15:41,280 --> 00:15:43,957
and that respect is going
to take you far But you also

284
00:15:44,040 --> 00:15:47,900
need to balance your deck with
magic and trap cards I do?

285
00:15:48,500 --> 00:15:53,440
Mm-hmm Matter of fact,
take this card You mean it?

286
00:15:53,620 --> 00:15:54,450
Of course

287
00:15:57,260 --> 00:16:00,497
Heart of the underdog It
reminds me of a good friend of

288
00:16:00,580 --> 00:16:03,960
mine And it could be just
what you need Can I keep it?

289
00:16:05,160 --> 00:16:09,800
No way Awesome Who does that
card remind you of anyway?

290
00:16:10,080 --> 00:16:11,620
I'll tell you later

291
00:16:12,660 --> 00:16:15,200
I'm going to test it out now Good luck

292
00:16:17,200 --> 00:16:21,100
I wouldn't set the level too high
If I were you Thanks, good call

293
00:16:21,680 --> 00:16:23,200
Let's try level two

294
00:16:27,380 --> 00:16:33,320
Looks like my plans in full bloom
are the sweet smell of revenge.

295
00:16:43,060 --> 00:16:44,360
Initiating gameplay.

296
00:16:45,220 --> 00:16:46,400
Let's duel!

297
00:16:46,800 --> 00:16:48,000
Commencing duel.

298
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:52,657
It looks like the Kuiper boys
forgot to pay their electric bill.

299
00:16:52,740 --> 00:16:55,557
Either that or there's still
some kinks in your system.

300
00:16:55,640 --> 00:16:56,699
That's impossible!

301
00:16:57,320 --> 00:16:59,760
We worked out every possible bug!

302
00:17:00,080 --> 00:17:01,760
Well, apparently you didn't.

303
00:17:02,100 --> 00:17:04,757
One bug must have somehow
slipped through the cracks.

304
00:17:04,840 --> 00:17:06,020
Stay calm, everyone.

305
00:17:06,280 --> 00:17:07,515
I'll figure this out!

306
00:17:09,960 --> 00:17:11,280
Get back on!

307
00:17:14,220 --> 00:17:15,160
We're trapped!

308
00:17:19,460 --> 00:17:22,320
Now altering original dual sequence.

309
00:17:22,740 --> 00:17:24,160
It's not responding!

310
00:17:24,500 --> 00:17:25,680
I've lost control!

311
00:17:26,100 --> 00:17:27,580
Step aside, Mokuba.

312
00:17:30,940 --> 00:17:33,580
Just as I suspected. What's the deal?

313
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:35,588
According to this analysis,

314
00:17:35,780 --> 00:17:39,557
your computerized card shark is
being controlled by an outside party.

315
00:17:39,640 --> 00:17:42,177
But we're not dealing
with any ordinary hacker.

316
00:17:42,260 --> 00:17:43,613
This is a high-end job.

317
00:17:43,960 --> 00:17:45,460
Who would do this?

318
00:17:45,660 --> 00:17:46,700
It's pointless.

319
00:17:47,100 --> 00:17:49,097
It's just an amusement park attraction.

320
00:17:49,180 --> 00:17:51,533
Why would someone want to break into it?

321
00:17:52,160 --> 00:17:56,631
Well, my guess is that they're using
it to get something they want from you.

322
00:17:57,140 --> 00:17:59,375
What makes them think it's gonna work?

323
00:17:59,520 --> 00:18:01,677
They got your attention, didn't they?

324
00:18:01,760 --> 00:18:04,417
I say we tear that scrap heap to shreds.

325
00:18:04,500 --> 00:18:05,330
I'm with you, bro.

326
00:18:05,413 --> 00:18:07,020
Let's go. Hold on.

327
00:18:07,280 --> 00:18:09,980
If you do that, we may
never get out of here.

328
00:18:10,580 --> 00:18:12,462
Then what are we supposed to do?

329
00:18:12,760 --> 00:18:16,819
The only way to get out of here is
to defeat that computer in a duel.

330
00:18:17,020 --> 00:18:20,657
So what you're saying is our fate is
in the hands of that kid up there.

331
00:18:20,740 --> 00:18:23,640
It's time to duel. Oh, no! Help!

332
00:18:23,920 --> 00:18:25,280
I can't do this alone.

333
00:18:25,780 --> 00:18:29,240
Now summoning berserk
gorilla to the playing field.

334
00:18:29,520 --> 00:18:31,460
Attack points 2,000.

335
00:18:31,980 --> 00:18:36,220
Supplementing monster with one
face-down card and concluding turn.

336
00:18:36,580 --> 00:18:38,200
That Jim's gonna crush him.

337
00:18:38,360 --> 00:18:40,200
He needs help. Hey, look!

338
00:18:40,400 --> 00:18:41,600
More bad news.

339
00:18:41,840 --> 00:18:44,546
The computer set itself
to the toughest level.

340
00:18:45,540 --> 00:18:47,480
Oh, man, I'm toast.

341
00:18:47,940 --> 00:18:48,800
He's right.

342
00:18:49,400 --> 00:18:51,540
He'll never survive level five.

343
00:18:51,820 --> 00:18:53,055
He's just a beginner.

344
00:18:53,500 --> 00:18:54,330
No way.

345
00:18:54,413 --> 00:18:57,097
And if Junior loses the
duel to that rust bucket,

346
00:18:57,180 --> 00:19:00,886
we're going to be trapped in this
place for who knows how long.

347
00:19:01,560 --> 00:19:03,620
Yugi, you know what we have to do.

348
00:19:05,640 --> 00:19:06,470
Yugi!

349
00:19:08,820 --> 00:19:09,650
Yugi!

350
00:19:12,800 --> 00:19:13,630
Hold on.

351
00:19:13,860 --> 00:19:15,213
I'll take it from here.

352
00:19:16,340 --> 00:19:17,437
Is that all right?

353
00:19:17,520 --> 00:19:24,040
It's cool Very well, I will bring your
deck to victory But you need to have faith

354
00:19:25,180 --> 00:19:26,760
Sounds good Now,

355
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:32,440
let's dismantle this thing
Go, Yugi We're all behind you

356
00:19:33,200 --> 00:19:34,030
Alright,

357
00:19:34,113 --> 00:19:39,200
let's duel I don't know who's behind this
But whoever it is, they must be stopped

358
00:19:40,200 --> 00:19:43,460
Make your move Or forfeit the duel
